Package: loongson3-cpufreq-dkms
Architecture: loong64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: CPUFreq driver for Loongson-3 processors (Rust, DKMS sources)
 This package provides the loongson3_cpufreq driver, taken from the Linux
 kernel source tree (drivers/cpufreq/loongson3_cpufreq.c) and rewritten in
 Rust for Linux, together with the scripts that set up the toolchain it
 needs.
 .
 The driver talks to the Loongson-3 platform management controller
 through the IOCSR SMC mailbox to discover the available frequency
 levels, switch the CPU frequency and enable DVFS and boost.  It
 registers itself as the "loongson3" cpufreq driver.
 .
 The platform device it binds to is registered unconditionally by
 arch/loongarch/power/platform.c, therefore the module only needs to be
 loaded on a Loongson-3 system whose CPU advertises the SCALEFREQ
 feature.
 .
 A Rust module cannot be built against a linux-headers package the way a
 C one can: it needs the kernel's compiled Rust abstractions and the very
 rustc the kernel was built with, because Rust mangles symbol names with a
 hash of the compiler.  The module is therefore not built automatically;
 run tools/setup-rfl.sh (no root needed) and then make, or see
 /usr/share/doc/loongson3-cpufreq-dkms/README.Debian.
